1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
What Wagtail actually is.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:09,869
By the end of this episode you will have Wagtail installed, a project created,

3
00:00:09,869 --> 00:00:14,186
and you will be logged into a real content management system.

4
00:00:14,186 --> 00:00:15,389
And then we stop.

5
00:00:15,389 --> 00:00:19,776
Because episode two reads every single file it just generated.

6
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:22,574
First, where Wagtail sits.

7
00:00:22,574 --> 00:00:26,953
Django is a web framework with no content editing at all.

8
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:30,564
WordPress is a PHP CMS with its own everything.

9
00:00:30,564 --> 00:00:36,942
Wagtail is in between: Django apps that add a page tree and a genuinely good editor

10
00:00:36,942 --> 00:00:39,554
on top of a normal Django project.

11
00:00:40,354 --> 00:00:43,834
A fair question: Django already has an admin.

12
00:00:43,834 --> 00:00:48,860
But the Django admin is a database table editor, built for staff.

13
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:51,722
Wagtail's admin is a publishing tool.

14
00:00:51,722 --> 00:00:56,439
Drafts, previews, workflow, a page hierarchy, image cropping.

15
00:00:56,439 --> 00:00:59,919
You would not hand a client the Django admin.

16
00:00:59,919 --> 00:01:01,852
You would hand them this.

17
00:01:02,652 --> 00:01:05,032
So here is the one sentence version.

18
00:01:05,032 --> 00:01:09,792
Wagtail is what you reach for when you would write a Django site anyway,

19
00:01:09,792 --> 00:01:13,758
but somebody who is not you needs to change the words on it.

20
00:01:14,558 --> 00:01:18,878
Start with an empty folder and a virtual environment.

21
00:01:18,878 --> 00:01:24,177
If you watched episode zero b, this is exactly what we practised.

22
00:01:24,177 --> 00:01:26,297
Make it, then activate it.

23
00:01:26,297 --> 00:01:29,639
Watch for the .venv prefix on the prompt.

24
00:01:29,639 --> 00:01:34,856
On Mac and Linux the activate line is source .venv/bin/activate.

25
00:01:35,656 --> 00:01:37,280
Now install Wagtail.

26
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:39,391
Watch the dependency list.

27
00:01:39,391 --> 00:01:40,771
Two worth naming.

28
00:01:40,771 --> 00:01:44,505
Treebeard, which is what stores the page tree.

29
00:01:44,505 --> 00:01:47,590
And Pillow, which is image processing,

30
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:52,786
so Wagtail can generate resized versions of whatever you upload.

31
00:01:53,586 --> 00:01:57,804
You might wonder why we pinned Django as well as Wagtail.

32
00:01:57,804 --> 00:02:03,131
Because Wagtail seven four only asks for Django five point two or newer,

33
00:02:03,131 --> 00:02:04,611
with no upper limit.

34
00:02:04,611 --> 00:02:08,755
Unpinned, you get whatever Django shipped most recently,

35
00:02:08,755 --> 00:02:13,194
and three episodes from now your screen stops matching mine.

36
00:02:13,194 --> 00:02:13,860
Pin both.

37
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:18,933
Check the version, then create the project.

38
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:20,126
One command.

39
00:02:20,926 --> 00:02:26,175
Those two arguments trip people up constantly, so let us be precise.

40
00:02:26,175 --> 00:02:29,957
Studio is the name of the Django project package.

41
00:02:29,957 --> 00:02:32,195
Ours is a design studio site.

42
00:02:32,195 --> 00:02:35,205
And site is the folder to create it in.

43
00:02:35,205 --> 00:02:40,840
Wagtail creates that folder for you, so you do not need to make it first.

44
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:45,930
And one warning that genuinely costs people an afternoon.

45
00:02:45,930 --> 00:02:48,188
Do not name your project site.

46
00:02:48,188 --> 00:02:51,876
Python already has a built in module called site,

47
00:02:51,876 --> 00:02:56,919
and shadowing it gives you import errors that make no sense at all.

48
00:02:56,919 --> 00:02:59,930
The same goes for test, json, and email.

49
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,188
The folder can be called site.

50
00:03:02,188 --> 00:03:03,618
The package cannot.

51
00:03:04,418 --> 00:03:06,421
Now build the database.

52
00:03:06,421 --> 00:03:10,166
And look at what goes past: 184 migrations,

53
00:03:10,166 --> 00:03:14,172
before you have written a single line of code.

54
00:03:14,172 --> 00:03:16,872
Those are Wagtail's own tables.

55
00:03:16,872 --> 00:03:21,140
Pages, images, documents, revisions, permissions.

56
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:25,279
And notice what you did not have to do.

57
00:03:25,279 --> 00:03:27,676
There is no database server.

58
00:03:27,676 --> 00:03:33,240
That created a file called db.sqlite3, right there in the folder.

59
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,551
SQLite ships inside Python.

60
00:03:35,551 --> 00:03:40,174
Postgres turns up in episode thirteen, and not before.

61
00:03:40,974 --> 00:03:42,417
Create your login.

62
00:03:42,417 --> 00:03:48,431
One thing that worries people: the password is invisible while you type it.

63
00:03:48,431 --> 00:03:50,195
Your keyboard is fine.

64
00:03:50,195 --> 00:03:52,440
Keep typing and press enter.

65
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,314
And run it.

66
00:03:54,314 --> 00:03:58,706
Your site is now live on port eight thousand.

67
00:03:59,506 --> 00:04:01,216
Two addresses matter.

68
00:04:01,216 --> 00:04:06,266
The site itself, which right now shows Wagtail's welcome page,

69
00:04:06,266 --> 00:04:09,117
and we delete that in episode four.

70
00:04:09,117 --> 00:04:11,397
And/admin, which is the CMS.

71
00:04:11,397 --> 00:04:15,388
Log in there with the superuser you just created.

72
00:04:16,188 --> 00:04:19,492
Open the pages section and notice something.

73
00:04:19,492 --> 00:04:21,144
A page already exists.

74
00:04:21,144 --> 00:04:25,499
You did not create it, and it did not come from a fixture.

75
00:04:25,499 --> 00:04:29,404
A migration made it, the first time you ran migrate.

76
00:04:29,404 --> 00:04:33,759
That file is one of the more surprising things in the box,

77
00:04:33,759 --> 00:04:35,862
and we open it next episode.

78
00:04:36,662 --> 00:04:37,601
Last thing.

79
00:04:37,601 --> 00:04:39,819
Put it in git, and tag it.

80
00:04:39,819 --> 00:04:45,707
Gitignore the virtual environment, the database and the media folder.

81
00:04:45,707 --> 00:04:50,144
Your content is yours; the code is what gets shared.

82
00:04:50,944 --> 00:04:55,232
We are leaving that generated project completely untouched,

83
00:04:55,232 --> 00:04:59,521
because next episode is a guided tour of exactly this tree.

84
00:04:59,521 --> 00:05:00,829
Twenty nine files.

85
00:05:00,829 --> 00:05:03,519
Most tutorials explain three of them.

86
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:08,098
We read all of them, including the ones you are told to ignore.

87
00:05:08,898 --> 00:05:15,469
Next episode, we open the box and read every file.

88
00:05:15,469 --> 00:05:18,098
Thanks for watching.
